# At 25 C the NTC is 10 kohm, matching r1, so A0 sits at half of the Nano's 5V pin (~2.38 V on USB)
# and the LED stays off. At 40 C the NTC drops to 5.279 kohm (B25/85 = 3977 K), pulling A0 to
# 65.45 % of 5V (~3.11 V) and lighting the LED. At 10 C it rises to 20.229 kohm (~1.57 V), off again.
open
step 100ms
expect @nano.A0 > 2.25V
expect @nano.A0 < 2.50V
expect @led1 off
expect serial contains "temp=25.0 C"
set temperature 40
step --until @led1 lit --timeout 150ms
step 50ms
expect @nano.A0 > 3.00V
expect @nano.A0 < 3.25V
expect @led1 lit
expect serial contains "temp=40.0 C"
set temperature 10
step --until @led1 off --timeout 150ms
step 50ms
expect @nano.A0 > 1.45V
expect @nano.A0 < 1.70V
expect @led1 off
expect serial contains "temp=10.0 C"
expect no diagnostics
